# Allowlist for `mypy.stubtest`, read by scripts/run-all-checks.sh and CI.
#
# The supported imports are "from host_cassini import ..." and
# "from host_cassini.oops import ...", so the stubs of those two packages describe the
# whole public API. host_cassini.oops imports the modules below, which are implementation
# detail and deliberately carry no stub; stubtest reports each as "failed to find stubs",
# which this file accepts. Nothing else is accepted: a public name missing from the two
# stubs still fails the check.
host_cassini\.oops\.iss
host_cassini\.oops\.uvis
host_cassini\.oops\.vims
